WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.938
This phone example performs two different tasks
First it removes

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:11.709
non-digit characters to create a digits-only
candidate Second it

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:17.511
checks whether the candidate has exactly ten digits
If it does not the

00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:23.832
validated ten-digit output becomes NULL Notice that
formatting normalization

00:00:23.858 --> 00:00:26.411
does not automatically make a phone number valid
